// A declaration no clause stands on is taught no lock: main has no callers,
// so nothing is proposed, although its body proves every absence. It was the
// positive control for "a body performing nothing still unlocks !Alloc" until
// T2 made a lock nothing stands on noise (2026-10-13); the locks that ARE
// stood on are tests/teach's lock-* fixtures.
fn main() = 42
